# The repository already stores every text file with LF. Saying so explicitly
# keeps the working copy on LF as well, so a checkout on Windows does not hand
# CRLF to editors and tools that then write it back into a diff.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Formats that are always binary, wherever they appear.
*.drc binary
*.glb binary
*.bin binary
*.fbx binary
*.png binary
*.jpg binary

# Fixtures are decoder input compared byte for byte, so git must not rewrite
# them. `-text` disables line-ending conversion without disabling diffs, which
# keeps the glTF fixtures reviewable while leaving their bytes untouched.
#
# This matters most for PLY and STL, which have both an ASCII and a binary
# flavour under one extension: marking those extensions `binary` would corrupt
# the ASCII fixtures, and leaving them to auto-detection would leave a fixture
# whose whole point is unusual line endings at the mercy of a heuristic.
testdata/** -text
fuzz/seeds/** -text
